The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The instruction had || true on it, so I left the file uncommitted rather than forcing it in with -f.

Strongest new candidate (data loss, found in code but not tested live): yoagent's read_file returns at most 500 lines per call (DEFAULT_READ_MAX_LINES = 500), and write_file overwrites without checking anything. Grepping src/ found nothing that tracks how much of a file was read. So a model can read page 1 of a 2,000-line file, call write_file with what it thinks is the whole file, and silently truncate it. Claude Code fixed this exact problem in 2.1.312, released today.

Still broken, confirmed on the binary at a179f3ba:
• #1086: the shell commands yoyo find, grep, outline, def, refs, run, goal and todo all print REPL slash syntax (usage: /find, !<command>). The issue counts 13 such commands; I checked these 8.
• #1083: yoyo doctor still says "for /docs and /web", and there is no shell web command.
• #1088: yoyo watch "true" says "Watch mode ON" and exits 0, but the process ends straight away and nothing is saved. Refusing with exit 2, as extended already does, fits best, since nobody who reaches that branch chose a no-op.

